From 8070f92f8b06a4d25f1a60d06b25f0c0bdd60097 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Schachter <davidschachter@appdevforall.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:13:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Measure the stack of the thread each call runs on

QuickJS measures the stack from the top it recorded on the thread that
created the runtime. A connection used on another thread, as in an
app's connection pool, failed at once with "Maximum call stack size
exceeded", or code that called itself without end was never stopped and
crashed the process; js_set_max_stack_size(0) was the workaround.

Each call into JavaScript from SQLite now calls JS_UpdateStackTop() for
its thread and keeps the size within what that thread's stack has left.
Nested calls (JavaScript running SQL that runs JavaScript) keep the
outer limit. Each thread's stack bounds are found once and cached in a
thread-local variable, since on Linux finding the main thread's stack
reads /proc/self/maps.
